# Definition of an m-Coherent ∞-Operad

## Setup

Let $\mathcal{O}^{\otimes} \to \mathrm{N}(\mathbf{Fin}_*)$ be a **unital** ∞-operad whose underlying ∞-category $\mathcal{O}$ is a **Kan complex** (i.e., an ∞-groupoid).

## Multi-Morphism Spaces

For objects $X_1, \dots, X_n, Y \in \mathcal{O}$, the **space of multi-morphisms** $\operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}(X_1, \dots, X_n;\, Y)$ is the Kan complex of *active* morphisms in $\mathcal{O}^{\otimes}$ from a lift $X \in \mathcal{O}^{\otimes}_{\langle n\rangle}$ (with inert images $X_i$) to $Y \in \mathcal{O}^{\otimes}_{\langle 1\rangle}$. Concretely, it is the homotopy fiber of
$$\operatorname{Map}_{\mathcal{O}^{\otimes}}(X,\, Y) \longrightarrow \prod_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{Map}_{\mathcal{O}}(X_i,\, Y)$$
over the tuple of inert maps, i.e., the space of $n$-ary operations $X_1 \otimes \cdots \otimes X_n \to Y$.

## The Partition Category

For a finite set $I = \{1, \dots, n\}$, define the **partition category** $\mathcal{P}(I)$:

- **Objects:** partitions $\mathbf{P} = (S_1, \dots, S_k)$ of $I$ into disjoint non-empty subsets.
- **Morphisms:** $\mathbf{P} \to \mathbf{Q}$ when $\mathbf{Q}$ **refines** $\mathbf{P}$ (every part of $\mathbf{Q}$ is contained in a part of $\mathbf{P}$).

The trivial partition (one part $\{1,\dots,n\}$) is the **initial object**; the discrete partition (all singletons) is the **terminal object**.

Let $\mathcal{P}_{\leq\, m}(I)$ be the full subcategory spanned by partitions in which **every part has cardinality at most $m$**.

## Decomposition Spaces

For a partition $\mathbf{P} = (S_1, \dots, S_k)$ of $\{1, \dots, n\}$ and objects $X_1, \dots, X_n, Y \in \mathcal{O}$, the **space of $\mathbf{P}$-decompositions** is:

$$\operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}^{\mathbf{P}}(X_1, \dots, X_n;\, Y) \;=\; \operatorname*{colim}_{(Z_1,\dots,Z_k)\,\in\,\mathcal{O}^k} \left(\prod_{j=1}^{k} \operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}\!\bigl(\{X_i\}_{i \in S_j};\, Z_j\bigr)\right) \times \operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}(Z_1, \dots, Z_k;\, Y).$$

This is the space of **factorizations of an $n$-ary operation through $\mathbf{P}$**: it consists of

- intermediate objects $Z_1, \dots, Z_k \in \mathcal{O}$,
- "inner" operations $f_j \in \operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}(\{X_i\}_{i \in S_j};\, Z_j)$ for each part $S_j$,
- an "outer" operation $g \in \operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}(Z_1, \dots, Z_k;\, Y)$,

all up to coherent homotopy. Since $\mathcal{O}$ is a Kan complex, the colimit over $\mathcal{O}^k$ is a homotopy colimit over an ∞-groupoid and is well-behaved.

**Functoriality.** A refinement $\mathbf{P} \to \mathbf{Q}$ induces a map $\operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}^{\mathbf{P}} \to \operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}^{\mathbf{Q}}$ by further decomposing each inner operation $f_j$ according to the sub-partition of $S_j$ induced by $\mathbf{Q}$. This makes $\operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}^{\bullet}$ a covariant functor on $\mathcal{P}_{\leq\, m}(\{1,\dots,n\})$.

**Composition map.** For each $\mathbf{P}$, there is a map $\operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}^{\mathbf{P}} \to \operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}$ sending a factorization $(Z_1,\dots,Z_k,\, f_1,\dots,f_k,\, g)$ to the composite operation $g \circ (f_1, \dots, f_k)$. These maps are compatible with refinements and induce a canonical map from the colimit:

$$\operatorname*{colim}_{\mathbf{P}\,\in\,\mathcal{P}_{\leq\,m}(\{1,\dots,n\})} \operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}^{\mathbf{P}}(X_1, \dots, X_n;\, Y) \;\longrightarrow\; \operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}(X_1, \dots, X_n;\, Y).$$

## The Definition

> **Definition (m-coherent ∞-operad).** The unital ∞-operad $\mathcal{O}^{\otimes}$ (with $\mathcal{O}$ a Kan complex) is **$m$-coherent** (for $m \geq 1$) if for every $n \geq 1$, every sequence $X_1, \dots, X_n \in \mathcal{O}$, and every $Y \in \mathcal{O}$, the canonical composition map
> $$\operatorname*{colim}_{\mathbf{P}\,\in\,\mathcal{P}_{\leq\,m}(\{1,\dots,n\})} \operatorname{Mul}_{\mathcal{O}}^{\mathbf{P}}(X_1, \dots, X_n;\, Y) \;\xrightarrow{\;\sim\;}\; \operatorname{Mul
